---
import Guide from '../layouts/Guide.astro';
import { services } from '../lib/repo';
import { site } from '../config';

const unverified = services().filter((s) => s.tested !== 'verified');
---
<Guide
  page="contribute"
  lede="Cupola is open source under the Apache License 2.0 and built in the open on GitHub. The single most useful thing you can send is a report from a service you run, whether it worked or not."
  related={['services', 'press', 'install']}
  get={false}
>
  <h2>Report from your own stack</h2>
  <p>Every integration is written to the service's official API and covered by tests that run offline. Whether it works against your instance, behind your proxy, with your certificates, is something only a real stack can say. These are not yet verified end to end:</p>
  <ul>
    {unverified.map((s) => (
      <li><a href={`/services/${s.id}/`}>{s.name}</a>: {s.tested === 'partial' ? 'partly verified' : 'recorded answers only'}</li>
    ))}
  </ul>
  <p><a href={`${site.issues}/new`} rel="noopener">Open an issue</a> with the service, its version, how you reach it, and what you saw. A report that says “it works” is as welcome as one that says it does not.</p>

  <h2>Accessibility</h2>
  <p>Dynamic Type, contrast, touch targets and screen-reader labels are held by tests, so a row that reads badly with VoiceOver or TalkBack is a bug. Please report it the same way.</p>

  <h2>Code and integrations</h2>
  <p>Open an issue first, so scope and direction are agreed before you write code. Setup, conventions and what a pull request needs are in <a href={site.contributing} rel="noopener">CONTRIBUTING.md</a>. The app has a written design system, with a rendered card for every widget, under <code>design/</code> in the repository.</p>

  <h2>Help other people find it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href={site.repo} rel="noopener">Star the repository</a>, so people searching GitHub see that it is alive.</li>
    <li>Tell the people who run the same stack: your Discord, your forum, the thread where someone asked for a Sonarr app.</li>
    <li>Writing about it? The <a href="/press/">press kit</a> has descriptions, the mark and the facts.</li>
    <li>If it is useful to you, a donation on <a href={site.kofi} rel="noopener">Ko-fi</a> helps keep it moving.</li>
  </ul>
</Guide>
